    "title": "Malden teacher, basketball coach accused of raping high school student - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Bryan Lambert ,\n3 hours ago Malden teacher, basketball coach charged with raping high school student A Malden school teacher and basketball coach has been arrested and is accused of raping a high school student.\nScott Marino, a teacher at the Linden STEAM Academy and the head coach of the Malden High School girls’ basketball team, was arrested by Stoneham police, Superintendent Timothy Sippel told Boston 25 News.\nThe Middlesex District Attorney’s Office tells Boston 25 that Marino is charged with two counts of rape, one count of indecent assault and battery and one count of furnishing alcohol to a person under the age of 21.\nLast Wednesday, February 18, Marino allegedly provided alcohol to and sexually assaulted an 18-year-old female who was known to him in Stoneham, the DA said.\nMarino has been placed on leave and the school district is fully cooperating with police and the Middlesex County District Attorney’s office.\n“I understand how upsetting and distressing this is to our community, given the serious nature of these allegations. We thank you for your continued commitment to our students and our district community. The safety of our students and staff is our highest priority,” Sippel said.\nMarino is scheduled to be arraigned tomorrow in Woburn District Court.\nDownload the FREE Boston 25 News app for breaking news alerts.\nFollow Boston 25 News on Facebook and Twitter . | Watch Boston 25 News NOW",
    "summary": "3 hours ago Malden teacher, basketball coach charged with raping high school student A Malden school teacher and basketball coach has been arrested and is accused of raping a high school student. Scott Marino, a teacher at the Linden STEAM Academy and the head coach of the Malden High School girls’ basketball team, was arrested by Stoneham police, Superintendent Timothy Sippel told Boston 25 News. Last Wednesday, February 18, Marino allegedly provided alcohol to and sexually assaulted an 18-year-old female who was known to him in Stoneham, the DA said.",
